\pard\sb0\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs32\cf1 CASE CONVERT\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 PURPOSE\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\b0\f0\fs20\cf0 Scans text for all-lowercase or all-uppercase words and shows what they would look like in other cases (uppercase, lowercase, title case, sentence case). Can also convert a specific word or phrase that you highlight and copy.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 HOW TO USE\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab Install the Phils Custom (cms) Checks plugin with Install_Phils_tools.exe. Everything comes with the plugin: nothing has to be copied into the cms folder.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab To convert a specific word: highlight it in Paratext and press Ctrl+C, then choose Tools > Phils Custom (cms) Checks..., select this check and click "Run...". In Paratext's check window, choose the books and set the options (Options...) before you click OK. The results will show all case variants for that word.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab To scan a passage for all-lower or all-upper words: leave the FilterWord option empty and run the check normally.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 4.\tab Review the results list for conversion suggestions.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 OPTIONS\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckLowercase\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 When Yes, flags words that are entirely lowercase and shows capitalized alternatives.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CheckUppercase\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 When Yes, flags words that are entirely uppercase and shows lowercase alternatives.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 MinLetters\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i 2}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Minimum number of letters a word must contain before it is flagged. Single-letter words like "a" or "I" are skipped by default.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 FilterWord\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i (empty)}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Enter a specific word or phrase here to see its case conversion options. If empty, the check scans all words in the passage. You can also populate this by highlighting text in Paratext and copying it to the clipboard before running the check.\par
